The geriatric claims that the deaths were not due to "lack of measures"
The owners of the Olot center do not eliminate the possibility that their night nurse has killed more than 11 elderly people
Managers of the geriatric La Caritat d'Olot (Girona) offered yesterday a press conference to highlight the damage caused to the institution by the criminal behavior of Joan Vila Dilmé, the nurse who killed at least eleven elderly people for whom he was responsible in the interval he worked there.
The director of the residence, Joan Sala, presented himself accompanied by the lawyer of the center, Joan Cañada and announced that "the desire of La Caritat would be to be able to exercise the accusation against the official" for the dead but "the legality and responsibility oblige us to assume the processual situation of civil officials".
And apart from the social discrepancy that the entity may suffer for not having detected in time the criminal activities of the night nurse, the great threat to La Caritat now takes the form of a significant compensation that the legal representatives of the parents of the victims are already calculating.
Joan Vila Dilmé confessed that the first crime dates from August 2009 and that from that day he did not stop killing.
The judge mentioned in the sentencing that he ordered the exhumation of eight bodies - former geriatrical patients - because he suspected that in many cases no doctor personally explored the deceased but, given the age and pathologies of patients, the formality took place by telephone.
Caritat, through its director, categorically denied this situation yesterday and mentioned that "the lack of measures cannot have been at any time the cause of what happened".
La Caritat’s lawyer added that “in this case there is only an indication of recklessness on the part of any other person that is not the accused.”
The person already baptized as the "Angel of Death" confessed the day beforthest 11 murders and detailed that he committed the first crime on August 29, 2009 and a month and a half later he killed a second grandmother.
In this case, he killed him by injecting an insulin sober-dose, unlike the first crime he had committed with a mix of sedative pellets.
The director of La Caritat mentioned the fact that it is difficult to control the access of the staff of the center to medicine.
Insulin injections and sedative cocktail had been the mechanism used in six of the nine crimes that the nurse, in his desire to relieve the suffering of the interns, used to kill them.
But the lab analyses will clarify if Vila does not lie by saying that he sought for his first victims a less cruel death or by the contrary he burned them inside by giving them laundry as he has already confessed that he did with the three women he killed in the interval 12 - 17 October.
Caritat does not believe the declarations of the nurse at night, nor the number of confessed assassinations, they do not eliminate the possibility that the number is greater and justify their attitude by the different versions that Vila has given in his visits to the Court of First Instance and the lack of logic in the change of how to kill after having successfully committed eight assassinations.
That is why they declare that they will remain at the disposal of the judiciary to clarify the scope of the facts.
