Eulen's president will challenge Vega Sicilia's counsel requested by his sons
The storm does not stop in the open conflict within the Álvarez family, owners of Eulen and El Enebro.
David Álvarez, founder of the group, will contest, because he considers it "null of law", the judicial council of El Enebro the next 16, solicited by five of his seven sons in which they will try to assert their majority and seize the management bodies of the incumbent firm of Bodegas Vega Sicilia.
David Álvarez and his sons Jesús David and María José grant their legal battery for the new chapter of their dispute for the control of one part of the group.
The founder of the largest business services holder for the companies does not seem to be willing to assign in his dispute to be present in El Enebro’s management bodies.
From its board of directors he has been excluded by five of his seven sons who have appointed themselves directors in the meeting of shareholders of January 18 this year whose dispute is registered in the Register of Commerce and Societies.
El Enebro's judicial council for the next 16, summoned by the Commercial Magistrate Number 2 of Madrid, has again opened thunder box within the Álvarez family.
The recourse of the judge to fix the assembly is, until the conflict resolves, the only mechanism that guarantees the convening of the assembly.
The latest movement of Juan Carlos, Pablo, Emilio, Marta and Elvira Álvarez Mezquiriz is described by David Álvarez as a "desperate remedy of the plaintiffs his five sons to try, through a processual argutia, by clearly defrauding the Law and abusing the law, to validate and correct the radically zero assembly on January 18", according to its official spokespersons.
This argument will be the basis so that, once the assembly takes place, is contested by considering that it is "null by right".
The same protagonists, who maintain a discreet silence, have already tried without success that the magistrate summons an assembly in June.
In El Enebro, a heritage company and holder of Bodegas Vega Sicilia, among other assets, David Álvarez’s sons control 100% of the capital.
The founder of the service group nevertheless solicits usufruct on 51% of the capital, according to familiar protocols.
This case is the question of substance that the judge must decide after the hearing on the request for challenge for which there is not yet a reported date.
Red Bull triumphs in F1 with a secret weapon from Siemens
Software creates improvements on real-time cars.
As soon as Red Bull entered the world of Formula 1 in 2004, its history in this select universe of speed was marked by surprise and success.
In the first moment, no one took into account the options of a new team that had just arrived, despite the upward trajectory of the last seasons, the past November, in the last phase of the championship they all bet on the triumph of Fernando Alonso's Ferrari.
Without lowering the skill as the driver of the champion, the German Sebastien Vette, nor the capacity of the Renault engine that propels his car, in the world of Formula 1 we speak of the legend of the "secret weapon" that the multinational company Siemens put in the hands of Red Bull to transform it into a winning team.
It is in fact a powerful process simulation software that the German company launched on the market in 2007 with objectives very far removed from the high automotional competition.
Named PLM, this powerful computing instrument has been used to create assembly lines from everyone's manufacturing factories, energy stations, high-precision instruments.
The objective is to reproduce, accurately simulate the product or process before constructing it in a real way, thus avoiding avoidable defects and costs.
PLM has facilitated the development of Canon cameras, Sukhoi aircraft or Nissan’s most famous commercial vehicles.
Siegfried Russwurm, head of Siemens’ industrial division, explains the fact that the use of this computer instrument in its Formula 1 factory has allowed Red Bull to create and execute “in a few hours, almost in reach time”, the modifications, changes and improvements detected during races and tests.
Russwurm explains that the 1992 teams had an average of 10 technicians in their teams who were able to introduce a maximum of three or four improvements on vehicles each season.
In the Red Bull team now work 180 high-qualifying young professionals who, equipped with powerful computer equipment analyze and project all sorts of modifications on the cars.
The manager of Siemens explained that the PLM software is able to analyze and improve all the elements of Red Bull cars except the engine, which is the exclusive responsibility of Renault.
Materials, fuel, aerodynamics, and safety elements are modified.
Changes can go from virtual reality from simulator to reality in less than 24 hours, thanks to advanced laser production systems and high-tech autoclaves.
As the only limitation of this madness of technological development there is the amount of 40 million dollars that each team of Formula 1 can spend as a limit each season to facilitate competition.
Red Bull set up the high-tech plant to create and produce its cars in a locality 50 kilometers from London.
There are two buildings where visits, especially for journalists, are restricted.
Everything that's going on there is considered "top-secret".
The staff for this assignment has 580 people, including two drivers, champion Vettel and Mark Webber.
Red Bull’s Formula 1 hero, arguably, is the recent champion Sebastian Vetell.
Among the immense technological resources that the brand of energy drinks has put at the service of its participation in the circuits, there are other hidden protagonists, whose activity is invaluable and zero notoriety.
The plant’s chief technology officer, Steve Nevey, says five years ago it could be said that R+D’s progress in the case of racing cars brought 50% of the victories and the drivers were responsible for the rest.
Today these percentages have changed and the technology represents the 85% of the success, while the pilots bring the 15% of the added value.
Nevey admits that the Vettel or Webber will never be replaced by computers, because "they are unpredictable gladiators".
HP will install in two years 20 clean stores with local distributors
Hewlett-Packard (HP) inaugurated in Barcelona its first exclusive store in collaboration with its partner Pont Reyes.
It will be the first network of 20 businesses between 80 and 100 square meters that the multinational plans to install in Spain for the next two years.
The company will account for this initiative with the 16 areas already present in multi-brand centers such as PC City, Carrefour, Saturn and El Corte Inglés.
The vice-president of HP Spain, Helena Herrero, gave as an example the redesigned store located on the Gran Vía of Barcelona, owned by Pont Reyes, with which she collaborated for 30 years.
The North American group prepared a plan to set up 200 brand outlets in Europe in 2013, a strategy that includes the 20 Spanish establishments.
The first open were those of Bucharest (Romania) and Belgrade (Serbia) last week, with the one in Barcelona being the third.
Herrero did not want to reveal the next possible stores, even if she confessed that Madrid could be the next destination.
The director of HM personal systems assured that the philosophy for the implementation of the stores will always be the same, with the support of a local distributor with experience and knowledge of the sector.
The North American group advises and deals with the design of exclusive store furniture (with products that can be touched in an interactive way), which in Europe will hold an identical image.
In addition, HP covers the training of institutional staff.
Helena Herrero denied that it is a franchise system and pointed out that the exclusive network of businesses purports to "improve the service offered to customers and SMEs in purchasing, assisting, post-sales and even packaging".
The Barcelona store includes a space with a world-class pioneering pilot program that solves the possible problems of HP’s computer equipment as a guarantee.
An online service connects with a technical center located in Maastricht (Holland).
"Thus, in 10 minutes we can solve problems that can often take even two days."
"This system is designed specifically for MPEs and users, because the major companies have already contracted technical assistance services," Helena Herrero said yesterday.
Sabadell bets on 'stelling' one million customers to its rivals in three years
More optimistic than other executives, Banco Sabadell’s managing director, Jaime Guardiola, thinks 2011 will be a hard year for the banking sector, but initially rejects a new liquidity crisis and predicts the end of the liability war.
Despite this, it foresees a collapse in the margins of interest, which one will try to partially compensate with increments of commissions and the price of credit.
Sabadell expects to capture in three years a million particular customers, his task at hand.
Sabadell has found a path to be exploited during the next three years and thus being able to survive in a very complicated economic environment.
The bank will launch in 2011 a new master plan that will hold a three-year lability.
The objective, apart from surviving without the need to resort to FROB's public subsidies, is to win a market by the capture of one million new private customers - 700,000 if we deduce those who can get out of the bank - his great task to accomplish, because until now this bank had spoiled more SMEs and companies than the particular customer.
This year it has captured 250,000 individual customers and 50,000 companies.
Its market rating to individuals is 3.5%, while to companies it exceeds 10%.
Another basis of the 2011-2013 plan is the bet on productivity, or what is the same, of austerity, with the reduction of costs as an objective, whose provocations will be explained by the bank when it presents the results of the exercise.
Few banks now dare to set targets and make them public, as the financial crisis has bothered all plans in the global banking sector.
Sabadell, in fact, will finalize his Optima master plan this year, establishes four years ago, even though initially the plan was for three years, but the market situation has determined its extension for one more exercise.
Clients who leave the savings banks will be his main goal.
During a breakfast hosted by APIE, Guardiola insisted that 2011 will be a "difficult and transcendental" year.
The executive, in fact, thinks that the end of the crisis in Spain "will be slow".
Moreover, in two or three years it will be "very difficult to create workstations", which is fundamental for the survival of the banking case, he insisted.
And even if he thinks that the war of liabilities - which penalizes margins - is shrinking, the price of risk premiums that banks and caisses are paying for its issues to obtain liquidity are already shifting to the price of credit to compensate for the fall in margins.
"The aspect of liquidity and financing is structural and will be a pressuring factor on credit."
“We didn’t tighten the faucet, but the differentials are higher,” Guardiola said.
Banesto has already given orders to its network to limit long-term credit and increase the price of differentials - see CincoDías on November 22 and 27.
He also confessed that the trend of the banking sector now "is to increase commissions", but "there is a competitive framework".
Sabadell’s master plan is based on organic growth even if, as always, the group does not eliminate the possibility of carrying out corporate operations.
It is not in vain that he assures that in Spain "will be solicited of larger dimensions."
“Everything will move next year,” he said.
He argues that capital necessities "increase enormously" and some Spanish financial entity could enter the red numbers.
And he mentions that the FROB can replace the market in casing funds in the case of new recapitalisations.
Having assured that Sabadell can survive the temporal closing of the markets, it has diminished the importance of the fact that some banks are already predicting as a new liquidity crisis.
He points out that we cannot issue, but on the contrary of what happened in June, we can obtain short-term funding through rest, which mitigates the crisis.
ECSC rejects the possibility of a second wave of mergers among the coffers
ECSC Managing Director José Antonio Olavarrieta yesterday rejected the possibility of a new wave of savings fund mergers and again insisted on the speed with which the restructuring of the sector is being implemented.
When the process of concentrating the Spanish savings banks began, there were several entities which assured that they would not participate in this first phase and that they reserved themselves for the second phase.
Nevertheless, the managing director of the Spanish Confederation of Savings Banks (ECSC), José Antonio Olavarrieta, yesterday rejected the possibility of the production of this new wave of operations.
"I think that most of the mergers have been carried out, it cannot be said that the incorporation of Cajasol in Banca Cívica's group is a second phase, these are adjustments."
"Most has been carried out completely; it is possible that instead of 17 we will go to 13 or 14, but all the major processes have already been carried out under the guardianship of the Bank of Spain, which has collaborated a lot in this operation too," he said.
In the declarations during a breakfast of the Aragón Association of Leaders and Executives (ADEA), Olavarrieta explained that the process of concentration is carried out "at the highest possible speed and we must be very satisfied with the way it is realized within the deadlines that have been fixed in the past, not now, in business plans with the Bank of Spain.
"The passage of 45 caisses with an average of 28,500 million volumes of assets at 17 with 75,500 million is an unmatched process in history, reducing the number of entities by 62% so that they are much larger to comply with Basel," he said.
Olavarrieta acknowledged that "there is a series of rather unhappily opinions about the slowness of the process" that demonstrate "a lack of serosity and meaning", because "what the Bank of Spain does is remember that we have to meet the deadline before the end of the year".
ECSC Managing Director José Antonio Olavarrieta said yesterday that Spain has the most rigorous financial system in all Europe and "probably" in the world and he has attributed to the people who question it a "lack of knowledge".
The leader mentioned that given the current economic situation, "we can remain very quiet" with the situation of financial entities and savings funds, a system that has begun a process of concentration "very important" and "goes at the greatest possible speed".
He also recalled that Spain's banking sector did well from the stress tests that BCE carried out in July.
Zapatero and the German Red Line
Berlin has opted to remain in the euro, but it has established the conditions for the entire Union.
Tensions in the markets have provoked a double government response.
On the one hand, José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero has announced new adjustment methods, which vary from tax reductions for SMEs, regulation of private placement agencies or abolition of 426 euros of assistance to the unemployed without professional contribution to the privatization of the 49% of AENA, the management of the airports of Barajas and El Prat and the 30% of the Lotteries of the State.
On the other hand, Vice-President Elena Salgado, with the support of former President Felipe González, is united to Chancellor Angela Merkel's criticism of her responsibility to detach the current crisis.
How should these movements be interpreted?
It should be mentioned that Merkel's position is not a mistake in her communicative policy.
On the contrary, it is another restriction of the difficult process of redefining the euro.
And there Germany has a radically new vision of what its future must be, which shocks with that of maintaining the old traditions of most of its partners.
Faced with European resistance, in Germany we begin to speculate on the three possible exits from the crisis.
The first, a strong euro, integrated by itself, Austria and Hollande, among other countries, and the south would abandon the monetary zone.
The second, the recovery of the Mark, even if now it seems science fiction, with a very favorable current of opinion, nearly a 50% of the population.
The third, a new conception of the euro, in line with the German proposals for greater macroeconomic control, budgetary rigour, fines to the countries that violate them, possible suspensions of payments from one of them and extension to the private sector the costs of potential adjustments.
The German position is clear and it has been defined for a long time, so now there is no place for excuses.
First, in 2009, when both IMF and the European Commission were stimulating deficits, the German government invented a constitutional reform to prevent them from 2016.
This was the first signal of divergence between what Germany thought we had to do (tax rigour plans and stability of public finances) and what its European partners, including France, practiced.
The second blow of the Central European country was when Merkel hardly extended the decision to save Greece.
From that moment it was the subject of fierce criticism, but the truth is that the political consensus in Germany and public opinion and published it were against the rescue of Greece.
Finally, towards the end of October, Merkel reiterates a clear position, asking the reform of the Union treaties to make possible the rescue of a country and at the same time oblige private lenders to bear a share of the cost.
This position has been interpreted as anti-European, as it precipitated the Irish crisis and the rest.
But his proposal, although slightly watered down, has been approved and, in the following months, we should attend the Union’s reform process that makes these measures possible from 2013.
Germany has drawn a red line she doesn't think she's crossing.
And it tells us all that, even if now we have to take measures with which we may not be too agreed, from that date the old functioning of the euro would have ended.
2013 will mean the birth of a new monetary zone, in which countries that break the rules will be severely sanctioned, they can be forced to declare themselves in default of payments and, in this case, the private sector will also bear part of the costs.
Germany points out that we have to follow a severe path of growth with high rates of savings and investment, moderation in consumption, improvements in productivity and competitiveness and positive external balances.
An alternative based on debt and construction, with huge holes in the balance of payments, such as the one that presided over Spanish growth in the boom years, will simply not be tolerated.
The bet is clear.
It would be wrong not to hear it.
It’s not just a question of renewing the public deficit by 3% in 2013.
What we're asked is much harder.
And what he absolutely must not do in these circumstances is to deceive ourselves.
I hope that the current turmoil leads to a greater tranquility towards us.
And that we know how to seize the opportunity that we were given, until the spring of 2013.
It seems that President Zapatero has also heard it from this form and his dual declaration (the reforms promised after the meeting of the past Saturday with the big companies and the announcement yesterday of the new measures) suggests that, despite Merkel's criticisms, we have opened the way to the thesis that it is necessary to put order at home.
But the red line that Germany traced is there, and they don’t seem to move it.
And among the possibilities that we are considering, we cannot exclude the possibility of abandoning a monetary zone that is too full of unserious countries.
And in that case, Germany will always be able to tell us that it had warned us about it.
Sport and Law Fraud
Ruses similar to that of Alonso and Ramos against Ajax demonstrate ingenuity but not the desire to escape punishment.
The expulsion wounded in principle by two Real Madrid players (Xabi Alonso and Sergio Ramos) during the match of November 23 against Ajax in the Champions League has caused a lot of ink on the anti-sporting nature of such behavior and whether both players should be sanctioned by UEFA.
As we know, a few minutes before finishing the game (which their team already made clear), the two players deliberately lost time when they made mistakes to determine the referee to show them the second yellow card.
Thus, and since Real Madrid will end up being leader of his group, the two players will perform the regulatory sanction during the next match of the play-of-war match against Auxerre and will be able to pass without cards to the next phase.
Finally, UEFA's disciplinary committee sanctioned with two matches the coach of the team, José Mourinho and various economic sums to the players involved.
The provocation of a yellow card in circumstances like this or similar is not a new practice, otherwise rather frequent in the world of football.
It is so prevalent that it is part of ethos, unwritten rules, but followed, of this sport.
Part of the debate that appeared in the related case is due to the fact that this has had as protagonist a team of the Entity of Real Madrid (which in its hymn displays nobility and honor and which on past occasions has fined its players for similar acts) and the dramatization orchestrated, it seems, by Mourinho, which adds an additional episode to its dilated history.
In any case, the debate asks whether this type of conduct not expressly prohibited by the regulation contradicts the principles of sport, that is to say, if with these actions one commits a fraud of law; because, indeed, they are respectful actions with the sporting regulations, but seem to evade its meaning.
The issue is to examine the type of harm they cause to sportsmanship.
One of the properties that includes sportsmanship is the physical integrity of the opposing players, an aspect that with these actions has not been endangered, i.e. there has been no violent gambling.
Another of these properties to which we allude with the correct game is to avoid that the team of infracting players benefits unfairly from the opposite team, which is not the case either.
However, the paradoxical fact of the action of Real Madrid players is that it does not agree with what is normally characterized as cheating or fraud of the law, because its violation of the rules has not been carried out in hiding to try to avoid the penalty, but their action has precisely tried to be as obvious as possible to receive the criminalization of the referee.
They were waiting and they gladly accepted the sanction.
Another question is the type of advantage that offenders get from the intentional faults examined.
Here it seems necessary to note that we do not put in a situation of disadvantage to the rival and we do not get an advantage in the same match either, because obviously the result of the action presupposes leaving their own team with fewer players.
And it’s not a useful strategy for the next match either, because the club couldn’t count on these players.
Obviously the advantage is that the players will start the next phase of the Champions League without cards that can threaten their participation in a future match.
But this is a long-term advantage, with a certain degree of indeterminacy, because the team could be eliminated suddenly and apart from that, with this action the players perform a penalty match and move on to the second cycle of cards, in which the suspension due to the accumulation of the boxes occurs with one less than in the first cycle.
So climbing the ladders is not so clear that this is an advantage.
Ultimately, these actions are not contrary to the sporting spirit, from which is still part of the making of strategic decisions that promote the maximum profit of what the rules allow.
In our case, players did not activate to avoid the application of the penalty (this would indeed be a clear case of fraud of the law), otherwise they chose rather the moment in which they submitted to it.
They made a strategic decision without thwarting the penalty or fleeing.
Even if the boundary between engineering and law fraud is diffuse, on this occasion I think we had a clear case of genius.
The controversy, it seems to me, appears because of two factors: because there have been two self-evictions and because of the way to pass on the director to provoke them.
The evil provoked by the principles of sport by these actions is not as ethical as aesthetic.
Offensive offers to capture Christmas dinners for groups in BCN
The dictatorship of the calendar this year concentrates an avalanche of bookings for days 16 and 17.
There is a proliferation of self-financing celebrations by employees who wish to spend between 20 and 30 euros.
Like the tuner and the lottery, when December arrives also return the dinners of groups before Christmas that continue to be the oxygen balloon for the restaurants and entertainment of Barcelona, but which because of the crisis have leaded to an offensive and adjusted prices to be able to capture the majority customer: almost all want to spend between 20 and 30 euros in dinners or meals, coincide the businessmen and associations of the sector interviewed.
To finish complicating accounting, this year's calendar (as Saint Sylvestre's night falls on Friday) concentrated the requests in the week of December 13, resulting so far in an avalanche of dinner reservations for peak days (17 and 17) and almost nothing the previous week.
Since 2008, which is the origin of difficult times, there are many companies that have eliminated collective dinners for budgetary reasons.
To maintain tradition, many employees organize them by paying with their own pockets.
Whatever the conjunctury, they are all asking for battle prices, confirms the president of Gremi de Restauració de Barcelona, Gaietà Farràs.
The employer's representative, now, does not dare to predict how the holidays will be this month.
"Peoples are thinking a lot before booking."
“They want to go out, but they pay a lot of attention to prices,” he said.
The case will go well "for those who give quality at a good price and with a good service", he adds, and recalls that customers have the tendency to go down a level with the crisis, so that the tranche around 25 euros has become the majority in demand.
In a survey in various establishments in the centre we see the collapse of applications for the night of 17.
The Soteras group indicates that there is an authentic demand boom for this Friday, with the pretension to spend less than 30 euros, to which they responded by adapting their menus to the conjuncture, with complete formulas from 25 to 35 euros.
In the case of another most powerful group, Andilana, with 16 establishments in the city (Hostal de la Rita, Market, La Fonda and others), the peculiarity of the calendar assumed more early bookings, even from the beginning of November.
"We did the impossible to maintain the same prices of last year, with menus for all tastes from 19.95 to 30 euros," they detail.
AN Grup, which includes El Mussol, Attic, QuQu and a total of 23 locals, remains optimistic after detecting a rise in billing since the second semester and good, albeit concentrated, business prospects for Christmas.
Sources of the group mention that 18 will also be a hyper-active day at the level of groups of friends who celebrate the holidays in advance.
To their six group menus they added one for Christmas, with 30 euros or more as a famous budget and the perception that there is a predisposition to spend 10% more than last year instead of requiring more details, such as Catalan wine made according to the Champagne method - 'cava'.
They also see the first signs of improvement in some companies invite their employees again and the feeling that the volume of groups has increased a little.
On the part of Fecasarm (which includes entities such as the Association of Bars, Restaurants and Entertainment of Barcelona), its vice-president, Enric Gomà, confides in the possibility of starting to see the finale of the tunnel and argues that overall bookings are "animated", even if customers "negotiate to the maximum".
This is true, hope for the festivities has not diminished, regardless of who pays, he says.
Pakistan's nuclear program generates great concern in the United States
Islamabad produces atomic weapons at "a faster pace than any other country."
Wikileaks filtration confirms the connection between the Taliban and Pakistan.
The content of correspondence between the U.S. Embassy in Pakistan and the U.S. State Department filtered by the Wikileaks portal confirms the huge concerns caused in Washington by the Pakistani nuclear program.
Apart from the illuminating and tasty details offered on the content of the conversations and thoughts of North American diplomatic representatives accredited to Islamabad, the documents reveal the fact that cooperation between the two countries in the field of atomic security, instead of increasing, "decreases" and that the unstable Asian country produces nuclear weapons "at a faster rate than any other country in the world".
The peculiarity of Pakistan's nuclear programme - the fact that weapons are unassembled, but they are stored by components to make it difficult to destroy them in the event of an attack - is one of the main reasons for concern in Washington.
This is how the ambassador to Pakistan, Anne W. Patterson, lists in a report before the visit of the former National Security Advisor, James Jones: "The proximity of certain nuclear facilities of the territory under Taliban attack, the dispersion of nuclear materials including the running noise and the vulnerability of the transportation of atomic materials."
The large number of people involved in nuclear arsenals and missile programs is envisioned, not only by the United States, but also by Russia, as proliferating and a reason to maintain custody.
“Pakistan had to hire staff with strict religious beliefs to protect nuclear facilities; given the decline in educational and cultural levels, extremist organizations have more opportunities to recruit people who work in nuclear or missile programs,” expert Yuri Korolev of the Russian Ministry of Externals said during a meeting with his U.S. counterparts.
The new documentation filtered by Julian Assange’s portal is the increasingly reduced cooperation between the United States and Pakistan in the field of nuclear proliferation and the high level of nuclear weapons production.
A dispatch from the Embassy in May, describing communication with Pakistan as "frustrating", argues: "Transparency is frequently non-existent; offers of aid remain unanswered or eliminated."
In another message, Peter Lavoy, National Intelligence Official for Southern Asia, said: “Despite the economic catastrophe, Pakistan is producing nuclear weapons at a faster pace than any other country in the world.”
Ambassador Patterson also asked Washington, during a visit by Army chief General Ashfaq Kayani, during a visit of General Ashfaq Kayani, to make it "very clear" for the official that "the Army of Pakistan must end with the tacit support of the terrorist groups".
At the hunt of Wikileaks leader
Obama will hire a senior anti-terrorist official to avoid new infiltrations.
Interpol issues a red alert to track movements and locate Assange.
All aspects related to Wikileaks and its founder, Julian Assange, forms a complicated labyrinth where it is difficult to have certainty about the facts.
Yesterday Interpol issued a "red alert" to "locate and follow the movements" of Assange.
However, this is not a traditional arrest order.
In addition, this one is not new, otherwise it dates from November 20.
And it has nothing to do with the latest filtration of more than a quarter million diplomatic documents of the United States but with the accusations of sexual abuse that the Australian faces in Sweden.
In addition, Wikileaks creative lawyer Mark Stephens said: “The police know where and how to contact Mr Assange.”
The 20 the international police force headquartered in Lyon (France) dictated order at the request of Sweden, but it did not make it public until yesterday, after having received the authorization of the authorities of that country.
For example, Interpol’s 188 countries have received an indication to identify or locate Assange “to obtain his provisional arrest and extradition.”
Even if Interpol can not give the order of arrest of an individual affected by a red alert, many of the member countries, according to the explanations of the organization, consider the red-notice call a clear route for the arrest - which the national police body must carry out -, especially if they have a bilateral extradition agreement, as is the case in Sweden and England, where it is believed that Assange is.
The movement outraged Assange’s lawyers, who yesterday published a letter denouncing that the 39-year-old Wikileaks founder has been willing to respond by video-conference to questions from Swedish authorities.
They also recall that Assange solicited and obtained the permit to leave Sweden's case, which is compared to the famous Lavrentiy Pavlovich Beria, Stalin's head of security.
"This seems to be a hunt, not a legal persecution," the letter said.
As the world searches for him – and in Australia his mother defends the innocence of his son — Assange continues to find himself in an unknown place, but he doesn’t care.
On Monday he gave an undetermined location an interview with the director of the magazine Time through Skype, a conversation in which he requested the resignation of U.S. Secretary of State Hillary Clinton.
"If we can show that she's been responsible for giving orders to U.S. graduates they're spying on at the U.N. by violating the international treaties that the U.S. has signed, it should resign," he said.
His opinion was insulted yesterday by White House press secretary Robert Gibbs, who called the request for resignation "ridiculous and absurd."
“I’m not at all sure why the opinion of a guy with a web page should be of interest to us,” he told CNN.
Obama himself has tasked a senior anti-terrorister official, Rusell Travers, to prevent further leaks of documents.
President Barack Obama’s spokesperson’s attempt to reduce Assange’s importance contrasts with the views that conservative politicians and commentators are proclaiming these days.
Peter King, the congressman who will chair the National Security Committee in the Lower House in January asked the State Department to explore the possibility of including Wikileaks in the list of terrorist organizations "to confiscate its funds and prosecute anyone who provides them with contributions or assistance."
Even further went Tom Flanagan, an adviser to Canadian President Stephen Harper, who had to come back on his statements after he said Assange should "be murdered."
"Obama should turn it into a goal and use an unmanned aircraft or something similar."
One who did not ask for an apology was Mike Huckabee, a Baptist minister, former governor of Arkansas and a possible presidential candidate.
"Whoever is in the government who has filtered the information is guilty of treason and everything that is not an execution would be too kind a punishment," he said.
Puigcercós seeks peace in ERC with nods to Carod's followers
The Republican leader will allow the party a secret vote on its continuity.
Huguet proposes a more plural executive and the end of the assembly system.
Joan Puigcercós seems to have found the recipe to solve the umpteenth internal revolt inside ERC, without north because of the loss of 11 deputies and half of the votes.
The president of the party is aware of the fact that his threat of resignation is not enough for the followers of the former leader Josep Lluís Carod-Rovira, but at the same time he knows that the influence of this sector is now as diluted as his liar and that this absolutely cannot give him headaches that he had with other currents extinguished.
That's why Esquerra's leader will try to win his new critics with winks that allow him to armour himself until the municipal elections.
To begin with, Puigcercós announced yesterday that more than 200 ERC's national advisers will be able to decide on its continuity in secret.
By ballot papers, not by raising your hand.
If carodists want to carry out a certain vote of penalization to the president, they will be able to do so without any fear of retaliation.
In fact, the rank leader wants to avoid the image of division and that of submission to his person.
In several interviews he stated that he would not consider himself ratified with half plus one of the votes, but he added, without mentioning the percentages, that a "Bulgarian-style" result would not be good either.
People close to Carod ask the president a little more than to make his position available to the militancy, a gesture not worth when Puigcercós controls the maximum body between the congresses.
But because they don’t have a sufficient majority to force resignations, they will try to agree with the executive a roadmap until May.
To this end, they hope to participate in the development of the strategic reorienting document that management will submit to the National Council for votation on 18.
His intention is to support Puigcercós in exchange for his promise to schedule the congress for the autumn of 2011, what the leaders see as a safe fact.
The ERC leader has confessed that "polyphony" affects stability and that his goal is that once and for all the organization is able to wash his laundry room with the family.
In this line, the article that the current advisor Josep Huguet signed in his blog results symptomatically.
Considered the ideologue of Puigcercós, Innovació's holder thought that the fact that the leader will be ratified "in exchange for various objectives" it is as if it had been done.
And he listed five, of which he emphasizes two.
The first, "recomposing" the executive so that it represents at least 90% of the militance, i.e
The second can be the character of great news.
Huguet proposes that ERC liquid once and for all the assembly as an operating mechanism.
Thus, he defends a reform of the statutes that allows the realization of congresses through delegates elected by suffrage.
Finishing with the assembly model, an exception in the Spanish party system, has been an obsession of the Puigcercós team, which has already struggled in this direction in the last two congresses.
In fact, the conclave convulse of 2008 instructed the management to revise the assembly model in a specific congression to reform the statutes.
This meeting remains unfinished, because the internal tide of recent years did not recommend addressing this topic.
Now, without critical sectors on the lookout, the time could be right to take it back and close it forever.
23 executed in November; 290 in 2010
According to MILENIO of the State of Mexico, there was a decrease of 4 cases compared to 2010.
In November 23 people were executed in the state of Mexico, four less than the previous month according to MILENIO of the State of Mexico.
Between the murders we mention these three women and the discovery of two cut bodies in Valle de México.
In the penultimate month of the year, there were 390 deaths in theory related to organized crime.
